-- title:
--   Proof of Theorem 1, p. 3349 — the pair (S^c, T^c) generated by steps (ii)–(iii) has joint pdf f^ex, for every offered wait z
-- statement:
--   Let $f$ be a joint pdf on $\mathbb R_+^2$, $z \ge 0$ an offered wait with positive patience tail $\bar F^{ex}_T(z) = \int_z^\infty f^{ex}_T > 0$, and $\psi^{en}$ as in (1). Draw $T \sim f^{ex}_T$ and $S \sim \psi^{en}(\cdot, z)$ independently, and generate $(S^c, T^c)$ from $(T, S)$ by steps (ii)–(iii) of the proof of Theorem 1 (kernel $\mu_{f,z}$). Then $(S^c, T^c)$ has joint pdf $f$: for every measurable $A \subseteq \mathbb R^2$,
--   $$\int \mu_{f,z}(t,s)(A)\; d\big(f^{ex}_T \otimes \psi^{en}(\cdot,z)\big)(t,s) = \int_A f(x,y)\,\mathbb I_{\{x,y \ge 0\}}\,dx\,dy.$$
--
--   Since the law of the coupled pair does not depend on the offered wait $z$, the coupled pairs are i.i.d. with joint pdf $f$ — which is the verification step of the proof of Theorem 1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** This is the per-customer computation, conditional on the offered wait $z$; the passage from it to the i.i.d. claim for the whole coupled sequence is not part of this statement. The case split follows steps (ii)–(iii) as printed ($t \le z$ abandons).
-- source:
--   Wu, Bassamboo & Perry, When service times depend on customers’ delays, Operations Research 70(6) (2022), p. 3349 (PDF 6), proof of Theorem 1, steps ii–iii and "Using basic computations …"

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DelayDep_Equiv_Model
import Definitions.Def_DelayDep_Equiv_CouplingKernel

namespace DelayDep.Equiv

open MeasureTheory

/-- Proof of Theorem 1, p. 3349, verification step for one customer with offered wait `z`: if
`T ~ f^ex_T` and `S ~ ψ^en(·, z)` are drawn independently and `(S^c, T^c)` is generated from
`(T, S)` by steps (ii)–(iii), then `(S^c, T^c)` has joint pdf `f^ex`, whatever `z`. -/
theorem coupling_kernel (f : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (hf : IsJointPdf f) (z : ℝ) (hz : 0 ≤ z)
    (htail : 0 < tailT f z) (A : Set (ℝ × ℝ)) (hA : MeasurableSet A) :
    ∫⁻ p, couplingMeasure f z p A ∂((pdfLaw (fTex f)).prod (pdfLaw (fun x => psiEn f x z))) =
      jointLaw f A := by sorry

end DelayDep.Equiv
